prepare the dolby vision recorder surface for hevc

classes7 mm/a0 (RecordProcessor) createVideoSurface builds a throw-away MediaRecorder to make the recorder input
surface. With the video codec on H.265 and the Video HDR item on Dolby Vision, com.oplus.feature.video.hlg10.support
reads false (mm/DV tenBit()) and it asked for MediaRecorder encoder 7 (Dolby Vision), which this phone does not
have:
  E MediaRecorder: prepare failed: -2147483648
  E OCAM_RecordProcessor: createVideoSurface, configure or prepare fail
  E CameraDeviceClient: endConfigure: Camera 0: Unsupported set of inputs/outputs provided
and the camera hung. With H.264 that branch was never reached. The surface is now always prepared as HEVC Main 10,
which is what the Dolby Vision recording uses (mm/DV over c2.qti.hevc.encoder). After: VID20261021213707.mp4,
hevc Main 10 arib-std-b67, DOVI profile 8 level 4, 9.8 s.

diff --git a/classes7/mm/a0.smali b/classes7/mm/a0.smali
index f83ad84..67e2757 100644
--- a/classes7/mm/a0.smali
+++ b/classes7/mm/a0.smali
@@ -17283,6 +17283,10 @@
     .line 292
     move-result v8
 
+    # createVideoSurface: never MediaRecorder encoder 7 (Dolby Vision), this phone has none and prepare() fails;
+    # the Dolby Vision recording itself is the HEVC Main 10 encoder (mm/DV), so prepare the surface for that
+    const/4 v8, 0x1
+
     .line 293
     if-eqz v8, :cond_149
 
